    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d702">

                <pb facs="0820" n="724" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg724"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Thomas.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic">June 5,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 55.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s No. 53 of the
                    5th and No. 54 of the 18th ultimo, I inclose copy of a dispatch from our consul
                    at Christiania, stating that the regulations for the inspection of imported
                    meats have been modified.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>



